This created the python module pyQtGnuplot, which contains embedded gnuplot
in PyQt.

To build it run:

    ./build-gnuplot-widget.sh

To do it by hand:

    # First you have to moc the *.h header files.
    moc QtGnuplotApplication.h -o moc_QtGnuplotApplication.cpp
    moc QtGnuplotEvent.h -o moc_QtGnuplotEvent.cpp
    moc QtGnuplotInstance.h -o moc_QtGnuplotInstance.cpp
    moc QtGnuplotScene.h -o moc_QtGnuplotScene.cpp
    moc QtGnuplotWidget.h -o moc_QtGnuplotWidget.cpp
    moc QtGnuplotWindow.h -o moc_QtGnuplotWindow.cpp
    moc gnuplotWidget.h -o moc_gnuplotWidget.cpp

    # Run configure.py
    # Check if directory $HOME/solps-gui/staging/share/sip/PyQt5 exists,
    # otherwise create it.
    python3 configure.py --verbose --sipdir="$HOME/solps-gui/staging/share/sip/PyQt5"

    # If on ITER load GCC module, so the newer gcc is loaded
    module load GCC
    # Compile and install the module
    make
    make install -j 4


The installation folder is in $(HOME)/solps-gui/staging/lib/site-packages/. To
change settings edit the configure.py file.

To import and use the module right away, either sorce setupenv.sh from solps-gui
root dir or append the path to ~/solps-gui/staging/lib/site-packages to
variable PYTHONPATH.
